# Cat and Dog Image Classification Using KNN

## Overview
This project uses the K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) algorithm
to classify images into two categories: cats and dogs.

## Technologies
- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Pillow
- Scikit-learn

## Methodology
1. Load the cat and dog image datasets.
2. Resize images to 32 x 32 pixels.
3. Convert RGB images into numerical feature vectors.
4. Train and evaluate the KNN classifier.
5. Compare Euclidean and Manhattan distance metrics.
6. Evaluate the results using accuracy and confusion matrices.

## Results
The project compares KNN classification performance using
Euclidean and Manhattan distance metrics.

See the accuracy_comparison.png and confusion_matrices.png
files for the visual results.

## Project Structure
- cats_and_dogs_filtered/ - Dataset and project scripts
- accuracy_comparison.png - Accuracy comparison graph
- confusion_matrices.png - Confusion matrix visualizations
- .gitignore - Files excluded from Git
- README.md - Project documentation

